   "evidence": "GPD/Kinematics.lean:146-162 constrains `n` only by `\u27ean, n\u27eb\u2098 = 0` and positive plus-momenta; `skewness_eq_div` (GPD/Kinematics.lean:225) is a ratio of two `\u27ean, \u00b7\u27eb\u2098` and `tMom` (GPD/Kinematics.lean:181) does not mention `n`, so both are invariant under `n \u21a6 c \u2022 n`, `c \u2260 0`. GTMD/Kinematics.lean:347 shows `c = 1` holds only for `ofLightFront 0 1 0`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/GTMD/Kinematics.lean",
   "fix": "Weaken to a scale: `lemma skewness_ofMomenta_eq (F : OffForwardKinematics 3 M) {c : \u211d} (hc : c \u2260 0) (hn : \u2200 q, \u27eaF.n, q\u27eb\u2098 = c * plusComponent q)`, and likewise for `deltaT_ofMomenta_eq` and `tMom_ofMomenta_eq`; `tMom_ofMomenta` then instantiates `c = 1`. The proofs carry over: the skewness ratio cancels `c` (`mul_div_mul_left`), and `plusComponent F.avgMomentum \u2260 0`, `plusComponent F.deltaOrthN = 0` follow from `hn` divided by `c`.",
   "issue": "`skewness_ofMomenta_eq` (L305), the private `deltaT_ofMomenta_eq` (L312) and `tMom_ofMomenta_eq` (L328) assume `hn : \u2200 q, \u27eaF.n, q\u27eb\u2098 = plusComponent q`, which by nondegeneracy of the Minkowski product forces `F.n = ofLightFront 0 1 0 = (e\u2080 - e\u2083)/\u221a2` exactly. `OffForwardKinematics` carries `n` unnormalized, and nothing on either side depends on its scale, so these main identification theorems are inapplicable to any other representative of the same direction, e.g. the usual `n = e\u2080 - e\u2083` with `\u27ean, q\u27eb\u2098 = \u221a2 \u00b7 q\u207a` (`minkowskiProduct_ofTimeAndSpatial_eq`).",
   "line": "328"
  }
